Why: the system package (0.14.3) is affected by CVE-2025-52887 (unbounded request headers,
memory exhaustion before the allowlist runs). This project pins >= 0.21 and vendors the header.
CMakeLists.txt refuses to configure if the sha256 of httplib.h does not match.

How it was verified (2026-11-13): downloaded httplib.h and LICENSE from
raw.githubusercontent.com/yhirose/cpp-httplib/v0.64.0/ ; the release publishes no checksum
assets, so the git blob ids computed locally with `git hash-object` were compared with the
blob ids that api.github.com returns for the tree of the tag's commit (they match, as do
the sizes: 859599 and 1075 bytes).

To update: pick a tag at least two weeks old, repeat the download and the blob comparison,
and change the three places (this file, the files, and EXPECTED_HTTPLIB_SHA256 in CMakeLists.txt).
Follow-up: orangepi/vision still uses the system cpp-httplib 0.14.3.
